The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says the merged reports are one issue with one fix queued.
Its own table says something else. Read the table, not the paragraph above it: every number
below is computed from `reports-4471.json`, the tenant directory and `causes.ts` at render time.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

<Callout kind="warn">
Two causes. The ticket owns the first. The second has no ticket of its own, so its fix is
queued nowhere.
</Callout>

## The two problems

**parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the
day first, so a date like 7 April becomes 4 July wherever the parser sees it: the app, email
and the booking-v2 form. This is what #4471 describes, and the queued fix is for it.
Filed as [ticket #1 · parser](https://github.com/egallardop13/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) in the repo this page ships in.

**hint.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. The tenant's people
type what the hint tells them, month first, and the form then reads it the tenant's way, day
first. Only the three booking-v3 tenants see it, and only through the form. Fixing the parser
does not touch it; the hint or the form's reading has to change. Filed as [ticket #2 · hint](https://github.com/egallardop13/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) in the
same repo.

Both groups look identical in a report body: a month flipped. They were merged on subject
line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), so nobody had to read the body,
and nobody checked which form the reporter uses.

## What intake got wrong

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant on file. The browser
is often not where the tenant is.

<IntakeCheck ticket={4471} />

## The footnote

The reports footnoted under `parser` in the table are the ones the desk read as a one-day move,
not a month flip. Their bodies say Tuesday became Monday, or two cities got two days for one
meeting. The desk's rule files them where their tenant puts them; engineering should read those
reports by hand before closing `parser`, because a one-day move is not what the queued fix fixes.

## How it ended

The desk's engineering update closed #4471 on 5 October. `parser` is fixed: `fix(dates): parse
dd/mm for eu locales`. `hint` is won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired, so nobody types a
month-first date into a day-first reader any more. Both tickets in the repo are closed to
match, the first as completed and the second as not planned.

## What to change on the desk

- Do not merge on subject alone during a date incident. Check the tenant's form first; the
  [dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) already knows the answer.
- A page that states a count should let a component count. The #4471 page typed "one issue"
  above a table that showed two.

